#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Space Invaders Infinity Gene cross-platform asset toolkit.

Confirmed by cross-checking the game files with the default.xex Ghidra export:
- Extracts BBX containers (magic 01 42 42 58), including unnamed and nested entries.
- Verifies the game-specific filename hash.
- Exports GMX geometry, hierarchy, materials and transform animations to glTF 2.0, with OBJ retained for static geometry.
- Decrypts the XOR-obfuscated systemfont CRP and exports its 2048x3392 glyph atlas.
- Extracts XACT3 XWB/XSB banks and wraps Xbox 360 XMA2 streams for FFmpeg/vgmstream conversion.
- Decodes text.bin and message.bin localization databases to UTF-8 CSV/JSON/text.
- Converts one-bit COL collision masks to PNG and standalone ANM frame-range tables to CSV/JSON.
- Decodes Bmap/Xmap 3D stage paths, wall strips, generator candidates, and Xbox 360 compiled shader containers/microcode.
- Decodes DAT command streams to timed semantic CSV/JSON, MAP byte-grid layers, atlas-backed previews, and a self-contained stage explorer.
- Accepts Xbox 360 STFS packages and PlayStation 3 PKG files directly, with bounded atomic extraction.
- Rebuilds extracted BBX archives, generates an offline asset browser, and supports the optional Blender importer.
- Produces deterministic output manifests, diagnostics, verification, and a built-in regression self-test.

Python 3.10+; standard library only.
"""

